-- Sequenced effects (ex13): `;`-batched effects share one statement barrier. Twin of 019-sequenced-effects.bqn.
-- Every batched effect reads the same pre-state, then commits at the barrier. This demo writes disjoint targets, so reversing its effects leaves the post-state unchanged.
-- Six pieces on a line, one under the cursor: Knockback shoves it, Flash tints it, Shielded drops — three effects in one breath. The Nords take gold and a blessing the same way.
-- Knockback and Flash are registered effect verbs (fn knockback pos / fn flash tint); ^cursor is a one-hot alias.
-- The .bqn's flash symbol column is registered as `tint`: an effect verb cannot share its target column's name (registry lookup is first-match). tint None/Red mirrors sNone/sRed.
-- Statement 2: rows 0 and 3 are Nord with TwoHanded > 60; row 2 has 90 but not Nord, row 5 has 99 but not Nord; row 1 keeps pre-existing Blessed.
-- The .bqn's reverse-order commutation witness and its `sel` binding are BQN-internal; this twin pins the post-state.
--! registry ../registries/019-sequenced-effects.reg
--! expect pos = 0 10 25 30 40 50
--! expect tint = None None Red None None None
--! expect shielded = 1 1 0 0 1 0
--! expect gold = 1005 10 15 1020 25 30
--! expect blessed = 1 1 0 1 0 0

^cursor , Knockback 5 ; Flash :Red ; -Shielded
Nord & TwoHanded > 60 , Gold += 1000 ; +Blessed
